        effect = "NO_SCHEDULE"

      }]



      metadata_options = {

        http_endpoint               = "enabled"

        http_tokens                 = "required"

        http_put_response_hop_limit = 1

      }

   



I don't have any thing in the eks_managed_node_group.

You hit two specific issues in this block: a syntax typo in your instance configuration and a missing explicit AMI type required by Kubernetes 1.30+.

1. Syntax Typo: instance_type vs instance_types
In your code block, you wrote instance_type = ["t3.medium"] (singular). The Terraform AWS EKS module expects instance_types (plural) as a list.

2. Missing ami_type for Kubernetes 1.30+
Because no ami_type was specified, your current module version fell back to the legacy AL2_x86_64 (Amazon Linux 2), which AWS has deprecated for EKS 1.30+, triggering your Requested AMI for this version 1.30 is not supported error.

Corrected Configuration
Add ami_type = "AL2023_x86_64_STANDARD" and fix the plural key name:

Terraform
eks_managed_node_groups = {
  system_nodes = {
    name           = "system-addons"
    
    # 1. Fix: Explicitly set Amazon Linux 2023 for EKS 1.30+
    ami_type       = "AL2023_x86_64_STANDARD"
    
    # 2. Fix: Must be instance_types (plural)
    instance_types = ["t3.medium"]
    
    min_size     = var.system_node_min
    max_size     = var.system_node_max
    desired_size = var.system_node_desired

    subnet_ids = var.subnet_ids

    labels = { "workload.type" = "system" }
    taints = [{
      key    = "CriticalAddonsOnly"
      value  = "true"
      effect = "NO_SCHEDULE"
    }]

    metadata_options = {
      http_endpoint               = "enabled"
      http_tokens                 = "required"
      http_put_response_hop_limit = 1
    }
  }
}
Alternative: Bottlerocket OS
If you prefer running Bottlerocket on your managed system nodes to match Karpenter's dynamic nodes, replace ami_type with:

Terraform
ami_type = "BOTTLEROCKET_x86_64"
platform = "bottlerocket"
